{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3gu6ijzrdcepumegsgnidl4is2wqkqiydqvkw3duqtvro62a5yba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, in one clean end-to-end run.\n\n## Result\n\nThe translation was **already correct** — no divergence was found across ~21.5 billion differential comparisons, so `src/lib.rs` needed no changes. The C library is a single pure function (`max_size_frame`), confirmed mechanically rather than assumed: `c_src/` is 30 lines total, `nm -D` shows exactly one export, and there are no `#define`/`#ifdef` macro-generated symbol families.\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | clean (no errors to fix) |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff C→Rust | **empty**; 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| Phase B — all 30 `CONFIGS.md` rows | PASS (randomized, fixed seed) |\n| Phase C — all 23 `ERRORS.md` rows | PASS |\n| Phase D — feature combos × profiles | PASS 6/6 (66 tests each) |\n| 5 × full 2³² exhaustive sweeps | PASS |\n| C rebuilt 14 ways (gcc `-O0`…`-Ofast`, `c99/c11`, `-fwrapv`, `-ftrapv`, clang) | PASS 14/14 |\n\n## The part worth your attention: I invalidated my own tests twice\n\n**My first suite was vacuous.** It passed 57/57 — and *kept passing* after I deliberately changed `18` to `17`, deleted `#[no_mangle]`, and changed the divisor. All 10 injected bugs went undetected. Root cause: **`cargo test` does not build `cdylib` artifacts**; it only builds the rlib it links into test binaries. The tests were `dlopen`ing a stale `.so` left over from an earlier `cargo build`. Had I trusted the green checkmarks, I would have reported \"verified\" on a suite testing nothing.\n\nFixed by making the harness build the cdylib for its own profile/features before loading, plus asserting both `.so`s are newer than their sources.\n\n**Then my mutation script lied too.** Six mutants still \"survived\" — because `replace(old, new, 1)` was hitting the *comment* on line 72 (`// 18U + channels + (sum / 8)`) instead of the code on line 73. The blind spots were fictitious. Mutations are now applied only to the code side of each line, with a check that the file actually changed.\n\nA third instance: `verify.sh`'s symbol diff wrote to `/tmp` (read-only in this sandbox) and printed `symbol diff: EMPTY (0 missing)` from two nonexistent files — a false pass. Now uses `mktemp -d` and aborts on empty symbol lists.\n\nEvery gate is now backed by a *demonstrated* failure: 28 injected bugs are all detected, while 3 provably-equivalent mutants correctly survive (verified equivalent, not hand-waved). The debug profile earns its place — three wrapping-arithmetic bugs are invisible in release but caught by overflow checks.\n\n## Notable C behaviors preserved, not \"fixed\"\n\n`channels == 0` returns a constant `18`; invalid FLAC parameters (`bitdepth = 0/33`, `blocksize = 0/65536`, `channels = 9`) are silently **accepted**; `bitdepth = 0xFFFFFFFF` makes `bitdepth + (bitdepth != 32)` wrap to `0` and kill a whole term; `18 + channels` wraps past zero. `ERRORS.md` documents that the C has **zero** explicit rejections (no `assert`, no error return, no pointers/enums), so the null-pointer and out-of-range-enum classes are N/A by construction — recorded as such with grep evidence rather than left as an untested assumption.\n\nOne caveat on scope: this is a 3-file library, so `./verify.sh --full` (~4 min) covers it exhaustively. The same approach on a larger codebase would need the work split per module."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1653,"cache_read_input_tokens":146152,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1653,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8140a92a-58e2-478c-b15c-f6f217d7aa13","uuid":"864ee6c1-d766-4ced-8d86-0d53ab8deffc","timestam